### 1\. Aim

To study and implement the Agile Software Project Lifecycle using Jira for project management, GitHub for source code management, and AWS Amplify for application hosting and deployment.

### 2\. Theory

Agile is a software development methodology in which a project is divided into small parts called iterations or sprints. Each sprint delivers a small working part of the software. Agile encourages continuous feedback, teamwork, testing, and improvement.

The Agile Software Project Lifecycle consists of the following stages:

* Requirement gathering: Collect and understand the requirements of the software project.

* Planning: Divide the project into tasks and plan the work to be completed during each sprint.

* Design and development: Design the application and write its source code.

* Testing: Test the application to identify and correct errors.

* Deployment: Make the completed application available to users.

* Review and feedback: Collect feedback, identify improvements, and plan the next sprint.

### Tools used

| Tool        | Purpose                                                                     |
| ----------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Jira        | Creates tasks, manages the backlog, tracks progress, and organizes sprints. |
| GitHub      | Stores source code and tracks changes using Git.                            |
| AWS Amplify | Hosts the web application and supports automated deployment from GitHub.    |

### Working of the integrated system

Jira

Plan tasks, create issues, track sprints

GitHub

Store code, commit changes, manage branches

AWS Amplify

Build and deploy the web application

Live Web Application

Application accessible through a hosting URL

Note: Jira and GitHub integration connects development activities with project tasks. AWS Amplify connects to the GitHub repository to build and deploy the application. These are separate integrations.

