* Check that the item contains `id`, `date`, `time`, and `timestamp`.

* Run the Lambda function twice and verify that two separate records are stored.

### Result

The AWS Lambda function was successfully created using Python and connected to Amazon DynamoDB. Each execution stores the current date and time in Indian Standard Time (IST) as a new database record.

